      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "If the velocity of an object is doubled, its Kinetic Energy increases by 4 times (KE ∝ v²).",
        "1 Horsepower (hp) = 746 Watts; this exact unit conversion is frequently tested in SSC and Railway exams.",
        "1 Commercial Unit of Electrical Energy (1 kWh) is equal to 3.6 × 10⁶ Joules.",
        "Relationship between Kinetic Energy and Momentum: KE = p² / (2m)."
